From: AROS Craft ports
Subject: [PATCH] rs_fs_open: the error of a failed open() on mainline ABIv1

Repository: rust-aros bf47cdfb60084264256399dd47fcf4a5dbd71dab, std-groundwork/libc-aros/csrc/compat.c.
Date: 2026-11-13
Problem: on mainline AROS (nightly 20261110) a failed open() leaves errno as an
  earlier call left it. posixc's __fdesc.c writes errno to its own stdc base,
  and since "stdc: make errno per thread" (956444232f, 2026-11-06) the calling
  thread's errno is the one of the first base the thread opened. std::fs::File::open
  of a missing file gave "File exists (os error 17)" after create_dir_all of an
  existing directory, or "No error (os error 0)"; code that asks for NotFound
  took the other branch (CADCraft: the workspace file was never written).
Rationale: errno is cleared before the call; when open() fails and leaves it
  clear, stat() of the path gives the reason (its own errno, or EEXIST for
  O_CREAT|O_EXCL, EISDIR, EACCES). Mainline x86_64 only (RS_AROS_ABIV1): ABIv11
  sets errno. The aarch64 target does not build this file and is not covered.
Upstream-status: the cause is in mainline posixc; fix to submit there.
Verification: cadcraft tests/tools/open-probe on mainline x86_64 nightly 20261110.
Removal: when the mainline SDK in use sets errno in open().
---
--- a/csrc/compat.c
+++ b/csrc/compat.c
@@ -666,12 +666,36 @@
 }
 
 #include "selector_aros.inc"
+
+#ifdef RS_AROS_ABIV1
+/* Mainline posixc writes the errno of a failed open() to its own stdc base instead of the
+ * calling thread's errno (since "stdc: make errno per thread", 956444232f, 2026-11-06; seen on
+ * the nightly 20261110): errno keeps whatever an earlier call left, so a missing file read as
+ * "File exists" or "No error". errno is cleared before the call; when the call fails and
+ * leaves it clear, the reason is taken from the path. With a fixed posixc errno is set and
+ * nothing here applies. */
+static int rs_open_errno(const char *p, int flags, mode_t mode) {
+    struct stat st;
+    int fd;
+    errno = 0;
+    fd = open(p, flags, mode);
+    if (fd < 0 && errno == 0) {
+        if (stat(p, &st) == 0)
+            errno = ((flags & O_CREAT) && (flags & O_EXCL)) ? EEXIST : S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) ? EISDIR : EACCES;
+        else if (errno == 0)
+            errno = ENOENT;
+    }
+    return fd;
+}
+#else
+#define rs_open_errno open
+#endif
 
 /* Names are distinct from CRT symbols: internal CRT calls cannot re-enter this gate. */
 int rs_fs_open(const char *p, int flags, ...) {
     mode_t mode = 0;
     if (flags & O_CREAT) { va_list ap; va_start(ap, flags); mode = (mode_t)va_arg(ap, int); va_end(ap); }
-    RS_FS(int, -1, open(p, flags, mode));
+    RS_FS(int, -1, rs_open_errno(p, flags, mode));
 }
 int rs_fs_stat(const char *p, struct stat *s) { RS_FS(int, -1, stat(p,s)); }
 int rs_fs_lstat(const char *p, struct stat *s) { RS_FS(int, -1, lstat(p,s)); }
